<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Thespiae</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Thespiae</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Boeotian city below Mount Helicon, whose seven hundred citizens stood with the Spartans at Thermopylae and which honoured Eros and the Muses.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Thespiae lay in the plain of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> below <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-helicon">Mount Helicon</a>. It developed in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> and became one of the larger Boeotian cities, often resisting the domination of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>. Its territory included the Valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muses">Muses</a> and the port of Creusis.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Thespiae's chief cult honoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eros">Eros</a>, whose statue by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praxiteles">Praxiteles</a> later drew visitors, and it held the Mouseia festival for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muses">Muses</a>. In 480 BCE seven hundred Thespians under Demophilus fought and died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thermopylae">Thermopylae</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> burned the city. Thespiae joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/boeotian-league">Boeotian League</a> but was frequently at odds with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> pulled down its walls in 423 BCE and destroyed it c. 373 BCE. Rebuilt under Macedonian protection, it continued as a cultural centre and passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 146 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thespiae.jpg" alt="Thespiae" width="320" height="163"><figcaption>Image: CNG, (uploaded by Odysses) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thespiae_431-424_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thespiae</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Demophilus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cults of Eros and the Muses</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Boeotian Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Greece</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thespiai</dd></dl></aside></div>

